    {
      "id": "cmps-2026-10-28",
      "title": "Cabinet CMPS — Container Manufacturing Promotion Scheme (₹10,000 Cr)",
      "date": "2026-10-28",
      "sector": "Container mfg / Logistics",
      "amountCr": 10000,
      "indigenousPct": 70,
      "summary": "On 28 Oct 2026 the Union Cabinet chaired by PM Modi approved the Container Manufacturing Promotion Scheme (CMPS): ₹10,000 Cr up to FY2039-40 (FY28–FY40: 3 yrs set-up + 10 yrs production support), announced in Budget 2026-27. Aim: lift domestic container capacity ~10x from ~70,000 TEUs to 7.5 lakh TEUs/yr and cut import dependence. Components: Interest Subvention ₹859 Cr (3% p.a. on term loans; greenfield ≥1,00,000 TEU/yr, brownfield ≥25,000 TEU within 3 yrs); Operational Expenditure Assistance ₹8,891 Cr per box sold to global standards (₹49,500/20ft, ₹86,625/40ft, ₹37,125–74,250 per 20ft specialised); Testing & certification ₹150 Cr (e.g. dynamic longitudinal impact testing); Scheme mgmt ₹100 Cr; Major-port land lease at 25% of notified rate. Local content ≥70% till FY2031-32, ≥90% from FY2032-33. Ancillaries named: corner castings, specialised steel, wooden frames/floors, paints. Demand drivers cited: global fleet replacement, Bharat Container Shipping Line, Vadhavan & Galathea Bay ports. Scheme support needs eligibility/approval by an Inter-Ministerial Steering Committee — not an automatic subsidy to any listed company.",
      "packages": [
        "Interest Subvention Assistance — ₹859 Cr (3% p.a.)",
        "Operational Expenditure Assistance (per-box) — ₹8,891 Cr",
        "Testing & certification — ₹150 Cr",
        "Scheme management — ₹100 Cr",
        "Major-port land lease at 25% of notified rate",
        "Local content 70% → 90% (from FY2032-33)",
        "Capacity ~70k → 7.5 lakh TEU/yr"
      ],
